&lt;p&gt;Learn more about our culture by visiting our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/culture&quot;&gt;Culture page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Review our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/trust/legal/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mentimeter is an engagement company with a simple goal: to make every leader better. Through interaction, insights and recommendations, its platform helps organizations turn participation into better understanding and stronger performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in Stockholm in 2012, Mentimeter is used by 20 million people each month across 1.3 million organizations. At Mentimeter, we believe better leadership starts with listening and that the strongest results are achieved together. That’s why we foster a culture built on curiosity, collaboration and shared ownership. By joining us, you’ll help leaders turn participation into deeper understanding and stronger performance, advancing our ambition to help more than one billion people listen, learn and work better together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As an SDR, you will contribute by generating new business by qualifying leads and driving various outbound campaigns. You will also focus on the development of each qualified lead to pass to your team of Account Executives and Relationship Managers. As an SDR you will learn and understand the key fundamentals of successful SaaS sales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a colleague with high energy, an entrepreneurial tempo, and the ability to work closely with our marketing and product colleagues, with a strong focus on business opportunities and sales. The ideal candidate is someone who can start relationships with some of the largest companies in the world - and move them from being loving Mentimeter users to large Enterprise customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are referencing the Dropbox and Slack journeys when we see the future of Mentimeter. Mentimeter is a service that is loved globally and our growth has been almost 100% organic. Sales are currently growing over 10% per month and you will be a driving force to accelerate that growth even further!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that a brilliant person with the right ambition can really leverage their time at Mentimeter. We are growing fast, and with us, so can you. Most importantly, we are looking for a candidate who is eager to develop Mentimeter as a company to a world-leading position. You will be one of the leading individuals making this happen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities for the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualify leads based on our user, presenter and customer databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deal with global organizations in over 220 different countries&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present and hand-over qualified leads to Account Executives and Relationship Managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve the processes, analysis, and tactics used by Mentimeter Sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect and qualify new leads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cold outreach to various prospects via phone, email, or Linkedin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work along side Account Executives to progress leads in the sales cycle and close deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasionally run meetings and demos for prospective clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resources we have to support you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Many (200+ million) users, presenters and customers who love Mentimeter&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional CRM and data gathering services (Salesforce &amp;amp; Salesloft) for advanced analytics, segmentation and outreach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;World-class lead-generation from the Marketing and Product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing and Sales teams to support in analysis, tactics strategy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentimeter principles / ways-of-working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation model:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strongly believe in the power of together, and we put a lot of effort into collaboration, teamwork and helping each other whenever needed. We believe that every part of Mentimeter, from Sales Development Representatives and Account Executives to Frontend developers and marketing managers contributes equally to our continued success. To foster and emphasize this culture and way of working, &lt;strong&gt;we apply a non-commission based salary model&lt;/strong&gt; in our sales roles, which has proven to be very successful and appreciated across the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The salary band for this role ranges from $65,000 CAD - $70,000 CAD annually. Salary will be based on level experience&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Read about our benefits &amp;amp; perks&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/benefits&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must haves for the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience ranging from either prospecting leads, cold-calling, qualifying leads, driving entries sales process, closing new business, researching good fit organizations and/or data driven market research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and some experience assessing business opportunities using data for informative decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial mindset&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ambitious and result-oriented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible mindset and open to new ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are required to have professional-level English - we sell to more than 220 countries globally today&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working as an SDR or BDR in the SaaS industry is a plus but not needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The recruitment process consists of:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personality test and logical ability test&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduction Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business Case&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competence Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentimeter follows a Hybrid Working Schedule - &lt;/strong&gt;you will be required to work out of our Downtown Toronto office 3 days a week (Monday, Wednesday and Thursday)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Mentimeter can offer&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Mentimeter we can offer a diverse and inclusive work environment supported by smart and driven colleagues. We believe in continuous professional development for all of our colleagues and therefore offer access to a leadership program (including external personal coach) and relevant education to ensure that we continue to be state-of-the-art when it comes to innovating and building Mentimeter. Your place will be in a growing company with lots of career opportunities, working on a beloved product used by more than 300 million people. It’s not all about work though, we also offer a very healthy view on work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All of this comes attached with a competitive compensation and benefits package, including pension contributions. Learn more about our benefits by visiting our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/benefits&quot;&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;AI and Hiring at Mentimeter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Mentimeter, we believe AI helps us work smarter - but it never replaces the human assessment, curiosity, and personal connection that define our culture and our hiring. We use AI as a sparring partner: to bounce ideas, bring new perspectives, support structure, and make our work more efficient. But the meaning, decisions, and interactions always come from people.&amp;nbsp;AI strengthens our work, but it does not define it. At Mentimeter, we’re not building an AI-driven hiring process - we’re building a people-first culture, where technology helps us listen, learn, and grow together.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture at Mentimeter&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Mentimeter we believe in giving everyone a voice - regardless of who you are. So we build a platform that does just that. Our platform is not only our product but also our organization. A platform where people feel safe, where differences are embraced, a place where you can have fun. We strongly encourage applicants who are people of color, LGBTQ+, women, people with disabilities, and/or formerly incarcerated people, and a college degree is not strictly required. In order to give everyone a voice, we need to be as diverse as our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about our culture by visiting our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/culture&quot;&gt;Culture page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Review our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/trust/legal/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mentimeter is an engagement company with a simple goal: to make every leader better. Through interaction, insights and recommendations, its platform helps organizations turn participation into better understanding and stronger performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in Stockholm in 2012, Mentimeter is used by 20 million people each month across 1.3 million organizations. At Mentimeter, we believe better leadership starts with listening and that the strongest results are achieved together. That’s why we foster a culture built on curiosity, collaboration and shared ownership. By joining us, you’ll help leaders turn participation into deeper understanding and stronger performance, advancing our ambition to help more than one billion people listen, learn and work better together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With our Engagement Suite in place, we’re continuing to strengthen the product organisation behind it. As Senior People Growth Catalyst (that’s what we call our People Partners at Mentimeter) for Product, you will help develop the leadership, team structures and people practices that support our next phase of growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join the Product leadership team, bringing a people perspective to decisions about team structure, leadership, performance and the capabilities we need next. Working closely with craft leaders across our Product department, you will connect our product ambitions with practical choices about how people and teams work and grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we scale our product organisation, there is plenty to build on: how careers develop across crafts, how we strengthen leadership capability, and how our people practices support an organisation that ships and learns every week. You will work with leaders to understand what is working, identify where we can do better and turn those insights into lasting improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be embedded in Product and part of the People Growth team within People &amp;amp; Culture, reporting to the People Growth Director.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an experienced People Partner who understands product organisations from the inside. You know how different crafts contribute, how cross-functional teams work, and what meaningful career development looks like for both individual contributors and managers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You bring strong people expertise, business understanding and sound judgment. You can easily move from organisational direction into the detail of a calibration session. You build trust, offer a clear perspective and are comfortable challenging senior leaders while remaining open to being challenged yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You work with autonomy: setting the approach when there isn’t one, managing several complex priorities and adjusting your plans without waiting for direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape Product’s people priorities:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and drive a people plan with the leadership team, connecting business priorities with leadership capability, skills, career development and succession.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help the organisation evolve:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with leaders on team structures, responsibilities and collaboration across crafts as our product ambitions develop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support performance and growth across Product:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead development cycles, calibration and salary reviews, building consistency across crafts and career tracks. Build on our shared people practices, adapting them to Product’s context and incorporating what we learn from each cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Coach directors and managers through everyday leadership and difficult people decisions, and help put our Heart &amp;amp; Bravery leadership manifesto into practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn insight into action:&lt;/strong&gt; Bring together people data, engagement feedback and what you learn across teams to identify priorities, agree actions and follow through on progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create productive leadership conversations:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and facilitate leadership sessions and offsites that help the group work through challenges, make decisions and move forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guide complex people matters:&lt;/strong&gt; Support leaders through sensitive employee matters and organisational change, working with People &amp;amp; Culture to ensure sound judgment and compliance with Swedish labour law.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in HR/People, including senior HRBP or People Partner experience working closely with product and engineering leadership in product-led tech companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across different product organisation setups, including helping an organisation adapt through growth or change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong practical expertise in performance management, calibration, development and salary reviews across different crafts and career tracks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating business priorities into organisational design, workforce planning and talent decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coaching and facilitation skills, with the confidence and judgment to challenge senior leaders constructively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid knowledge of Swedish labour law and experience supporting organisational change, including MBL consultation processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication in English and the ability to make complex people topics understandable and useful to different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using data and AI to improve how you work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation at Mentimeter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mentimeter, we believe in fair and transparent compensation that grows with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The salary range for this role is SEK 65,000–74,000 per month. The range reflects where you are within this stage of the role: your relevant experience, demonstrated skills, and alignment with what the role requires. As you develop and take on more, your salary and level evolve with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re committed to supporting your growth. You&#39;ll have ongoing development conversations with your manager, and your salary will evolve as you build skills and contribute to our mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to your monthly salary, we offer a comprehensive benefits package—learn more about it here:&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/benefits/stockholm&quot;&gt; https://www.mentimeter.com/benefits/stockholm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Mentimeter can offer&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Mentimeter we can offer a diverse and inclusive work environment supported by smart and driven colleagues. We believe in continuous professional development for all of our colleagues and therefore offer access to a leadership program (including external personal coach) and relevant education to ensure that we continue to be state-of-the-art when it comes to innovating and building Mentimeter. Your place will be in a growing company with lots of career opportunities, working on a beloved product used by more than 300 million people. It’s not all about work though, we also offer a very healthy view on work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All of this comes attached with a competitive compensation and benefits package, including pension contributions. Learn more about our benefits by visiting our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/benefits&quot;&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;AI and Hiring at Mentimeter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Mentimeter, we believe AI helps us work smarter - but it never replaces the human assessment, curiosity, and personal connection that define our culture and our hiring. We use AI as a sparring partner: to bounce ideas, bring new perspectives, support structure, and make our work more efficient. But the meaning, decisions, and interactions always come from people.&amp;nbsp;AI strengthens our work, but it does not define it. At Mentimeter, we’re not building an AI-driven hiring process - we’re building a people-first culture, where technology helps us listen, learn, and grow together.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture at Mentimeter&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Mentimeter we believe in giving everyone a voice - regardless of who you are. So we build a platform that does just that. Our platform is not only our product but also our organization. A platform where people feel safe, where differences are embraced, a place where you can have fun. We strongly encourage applicants who are people of color, LGBTQ+, women, people with disabilities, and/or formerly incarcerated people, and a college degree is not strictly required. In order to give everyone a voice, we need to be as diverse as our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about our culture by visiting our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/culture&quot;&gt;Culture page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Review our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/trust/legal/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mentimeter is an engagement company with a simple goal: to make every leader better. Through interaction, insights and recommendations, its platform helps organizations turn participation into better understanding and stronger performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in Stockholm in 2012, Mentimeter is used by 20 million people each month across 1.3 million organizations. At Mentimeter, we believe better leadership starts with listening and that the strongest results are achieved together. That’s why we foster a culture built on curiosity, collaboration and shared ownership. By joining us, you’ll help leaders turn participation into deeper understanding and stronger performance, advancing our ambition to help more than one billion people listen, learn and work better together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Designer at Mentimeter, you own the experience your team ships and how it fits into the whole: making sure it works, solves a problem people actually have, and holds together as we build more. Millions of leaders use Mentimeter to lead: to make a decision, bring people with them, understand what their organisation actually thinks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You join at the point where the work gets hardest and most interesting. Mentimeter has grown from one tool into an engagement suite, and making those pieces feel like one experience leaders and organisations can build on is now one of our hardest problems. The payoff is turning a great moment of engagement into results people act on, insight that holds over time, and value that spreads across an organisation, powered by AI that helps leaders see what matters and act on it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll report to the Design Director for that area and work day to day inside a product team, alongside a Product Manager and Product Engineers. Beyond the team, you’ll work with other competences such as User Research, Analytics, Content Design, Accessibility, Design Systems, Marketing and Sales to understand users and keep the suite coherent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design end-to-end experiences across the full development model, from problem framing through shipped and refined iteration: interaction, visual design, usability, prototyping and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take an ambiguous problem and leave the room with a clear problem statement, hypotheses and success criteria you can evaluate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ground direction in user evidence. Spend real time with users, read the signal, and read the release data afterwards to know whether anything actually changed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Name the trade-offs between user value, usability, coherence and technical constraint instead of letting them sit implicit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design patterns that scale across surfaces and teams, and protect product-wide coherence as the suite grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You own the experience, not the handoff. You work from the problem through to what shipped and what it changed, and you treat &quot;did this work for the user?&quot; as part of your job, not someone else&#39;s follow-up. You can hold a strong design opinion without needing to win the room, and you’d rather get to the right solution to the right problem than polish the wrong one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You work through AI as part of how you design, not a tool you reach for occasionally. You use it across research, exploration and execution, you read its output critically rather than ship it, and you hold a real view of where it strengthens the work and where it degrades the experience. Autocomplete is not what we mean.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You treat insight and data as design material, not reporting. You&#39;re comfortable close to users and close to the numbers, and you bring the team closer to both.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;This role might not be for you if…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use AI only as autocomplete, or steer clear of it, rather than making it part of how you design and solve problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want the problem handed to you fully framed, with the user need and success criteria already decided.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You see design as what happens after the real decisions are made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You treat research and data as someone else&#39;s job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You consider the work done when the design ships, rather than when you know whether it changed something for users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to stay in visual polish and avoid the ambiguity of early product work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio that shows end-to-end product design: problem framing, interaction and visual craft, and shipped outcomes, not only final screens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence that you ground design in user research and data, and change direction based on what you learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI built into how you already work, across research, exploration and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product thinking: you frame design decisions in terms of user value, business impact and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems awareness: you design patterns that hold across surfaces and teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, and comfort working independently and in a cross-functional team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t have to know Swedish. Daily work is carried out in English and the Mentimeter team currently boasts over 50 nationalities!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is primarily an on-site role at Mentimeter HQ in Stockholm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Mentimeter, we believe in fair and transparent compensation that grows with you. The salary range for this role is SEK 65,000–SEK 82,000 per month. It’s intentionally broad to reflect the different stages of growth within the role: from early development to deep expertise and meaningful impact.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Where an individual is placed within the range depends on factors such as relevant experience, demonstrated skills, and alignment with the role’s requirements. We’re committed to supporting your growth. You’ll have ongoing development conversations with your manager, and your salary will evolve as you build skills and contribute to our mission.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;In addition to your monthly salary, we offer a comprehensive benefits package—learn more about it here: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;https://www.mentimeter.com/benefits/stockholm&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Mentimeter can offer&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Mentimeter we can offer a diverse and inclusive work environment supported by smart and driven colleagues. We believe in continuous professional development for all of our colleagues and therefore offer access to a leadership program (including external personal coach) and relevant education to ensure that we continue to be state-of-the-art when it comes to innovating and building Mentimeter. Your place will be in a growing company with lots of career opportunities, working on a beloved product used by more than 300 million people. It’s not all about work though, we also offer a very healthy view on work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All of this comes attached with a competitive compensation and benefits package, including pension contributions. Learn more about our benefits by visiting our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/benefits&quot;&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;AI and Hiring at Mentimeter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Mentimeter, we believe AI helps us work smarter - but it never replaces the human assessment, curiosity, and personal connection that define our culture and our hiring. We use AI as a sparring partner: to bounce ideas, bring new perspectives, support structure, and make our work more efficient. But the meaning, decisions, and interactions always come from people.&amp;nbsp;AI strengthens our work, but it does not define it. At Mentimeter, we’re not building an AI-driven hiring process - we’re building a people-first culture, where technology helps us listen, learn, and grow together.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture at Mentimeter&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Mentimeter we believe in giving everyone a voice - regardless of who you are. So we build a platform that does just that. Our platform is not only our product but also our organization. A platform where people feel safe, where differences are embraced, a place where you can have fun. We strongly encourage applicants who are people of color, LGBTQ+, women, people with disabilities, and/or formerly incarcerated people, and a college degree is not strictly required. In order to give everyone a voice, we need to be as diverse as our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about our culture by visiting our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/culture&quot;&gt;Culture page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Review our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/trust/legal/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mentimeter is an engagement company with a simple goal: to make every leader better. Through interaction, insights and recommendations, its platform helps organizations turn participation into better understanding and stronger performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in Stockholm in 2012, Mentimeter is used by 20 million people each month across 1.3 million organizations. At Mentimeter, we believe better leadership starts with listening and that the strongest results are achieved together. That’s why we foster a culture built on curiosity, collaboration and shared ownership. By joining us, you’ll help leaders turn participation into deeper understanding and stronger performance, advancing our ambition to help more than one billion people listen, learn and work better together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is changing how people create and consume content, and the Insights product area is where Mentimeter turns that shift into an advantage rather than something we retrofit later. It&#39;s the area that decides what every one of our users sees, learns and does next, to turn data into something valuable enough to come back for, and in turn drive retention and expansion for our business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Product Manager, Data / ML, you&#39;ll own the data and ML depth of Insights: the intelligence that turns every interaction into sharper results, insights and recommendations, pulls in context from inside and outside Mentimeter, and gets better the more it&#39;s used. With 300 million users&#39; worth of interaction data behind it, the mandate is to turn that into a defensible asset. The data and ML is the means; a system that drives measurable outcomes for users and the business is the end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior, hands-on role with a clear mandate. You&#39;ll report to the Product Director of Insights: the Director owns the area&#39;s place in company strategy and its org shape, while you own the data and ML depth that delivers it. You&#39;ll work alongside the other product managers in the area, our Staff Engineers, our Science Lead, the Office of the CTO, and our data platform teams. The exact shape of the teams is still forming, and you&#39;ll help shape it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first year, success looks like a clear direction the area is bought into, and the first solid evidence that the system is compounding.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the data and ML direction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the data and ML direction for the area and get alignment behind it across product, engineering and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn raw interaction data into immediately useful, actionable insight for users, at the individual level and aggregated up to the organization, measured by whether people come back and act on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep recommendations grounded in science, not just patterns in the data, working closely with our Science Lead to keep what we surface credible and defensible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the intelligence platform, for UI and agents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the platform that generates insights and recommendations: opinionated, grounded in our thought leadership, and built so the rest of the suite can build on top of it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make that intelligence usable two ways at once, surfaced directly in Mentimeter&#39;s UI and exposed so our AI companion and external agents can act on it, with a clean separation between the logic and context layer and the experience layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the ranking and timing that gets the right insight to the right user at the right moment, getting sharper from what lands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Staff Engineers on the architecture and technical bets: you bring the product judgment and the outcomes the system must serve, they own the technical design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make it learn, and prove it&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the measurement and experimentation standards the area scales by, so we only scale what shows durable lift against a strong baseline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Show, with evidence, how the system&#39;s insights and recommendations get sharper over time as it learns from feedback, for example through reinforcement learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own how we ship AI well: anticipate failure modes, set quality bars, guard against feedback loops that reinforce errors, and roll back cleanly when the model is wrong.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make pragmatic calls on when to reach for ML, GenAI or something simpler, proving value before scaling.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An experienced data / AI product leader&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years leading data-driven or ML-backed products end to end, from discovery through rollout, ideally in B2B SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with recommendation engines or similar ranking and personalization systems is highly relevant, and familiarity with AI ecosystems and integration patterns such as MCP is a bonus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You build the data system, not just the surface&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve shipped data or AI products where the core value is the system itself, and you&#39;re comfortable reasoning about pipelines, models, and how data compounds over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve led shared-capability or platform work where the real win was adoption and alignment across teams, not just shipping features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercially minded and outcome-driven&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You connect product decisions to business outcomes like retention, expansion and durable engagement, and treat data and ML as how you get there, not the point in itself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a bias for the simplest solution that works, you resist over-engineering, and you have good judgment on when advanced ML or GenAI is worth the trade-off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rigorous and AI-native&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong on experimentation, with real fluency in A/B testing, incrementality and causal inference.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in shipping AI responsibly and well: eval sets, failure modes, and a clear sense of what &quot;good enough&quot; looks like before something goes live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A leader who multiplies others&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You lead through influence and coaching, make progress in ambiguity through iterative learning and clear decision points, and bring out the best in the people around you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet 100% of our qualifications? Please apply anyway and let us know why you&#39;d enjoy working in this role at Mentimeter.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practical details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role is based in our Stockholm office, primarily onsite with the option to work from home twice per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Swedish is not required. Daily work is carried out in English, and the Mentimeter team currently boasts 50+ nationalities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A cover letter is not required as part of your application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Mentimeter, we believe in fair and transparent compensation that grows with you. The salary range for this role is SEK 70,000–SEK 91,000 per month. It’s intentionally broad to reflect the different stages of growth within the role: from early development to deep expertise and meaningful impact.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Where an individual is placed within the range depends on factors such as relevant experience, demonstrated skills, and alignment with the role’s requirements. We’re committed to supporting your growth. You’ll have ongoing development conversations with your manager, and your salary will evolve as you build skills and contribute to our mission.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;In addition to your monthly salary, we offer a comprehensive benefits package—learn more about it here: &lt;/em&gt;https://www.mentimeter.com/benefits/stockholm&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Mentimeter can offer&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Mentimeter we can offer a diverse and inclusive work environment supported by smart and driven colleagues. We believe in continuous professional development for all of our colleagues and therefore offer access to a leadership program (including external personal coach) and relevant education to ensure that we continue to be state-of-the-art when it comes to innovating and building Mentimeter. Your place will be in a growing company with lots of career opportunities, working on a beloved product used by more than 300 million people. It’s not all about work though, we also offer a very healthy view on work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All of this comes attached with a competitive compensation and benefits package, including pension contributions. Learn more about our benefits by visiting our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/benefits&quot;&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;AI and Hiring at Mentimeter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Mentimeter, we believe AI helps us work smarter - but it never replaces the human assessment, curiosity, and personal connection that define our culture and our hiring. We use AI as a sparring partner: to bounce ideas, bring new perspectives, support structure, and make our work more efficient. But the meaning, decisions, and interactions always come from people.&amp;nbsp;AI strengthens our work, but it does not define it. At Mentimeter, we’re not building an AI-driven hiring process - we’re building a people-first culture, where technology helps us listen, learn, and grow together.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture at Mentimeter&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Mentimeter we believe in giving everyone a voice - regardless of who you are. So we build a platform that does just that. Our platform is not only our product but also our organization. A platform where people feel safe, where differences are embraced, a place where you can have fun. We strongly encourage applicants who are people of color, LGBTQ+, women, people with disabilities, and/or formerly incarcerated people, and a college degree is not strictly required. In order to give everyone a voice, we need to be as diverse as our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about our culture by visiting our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/culture&quot;&gt;Culture page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Review our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/trust/legal/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mentimeter is an engagement company with a simple goal: to make every leader better. Through interaction, insights and recommendations, its platform helps organizations turn participation into better understanding and stronger performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in Stockholm in 2012, Mentimeter is used by 20 million people each month across 1.3 million organizations. At Mentimeter, we believe better leadership starts with listening and that the strongest results are achieved together. That’s why we foster a culture built on curiosity, collaboration and shared ownership. By joining us, you’ll help leaders turn participation into deeper understanding and stronger performance, advancing our ambition to help more than one billion people listen, learn and work better together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Mentimeter&#39;s enterprise growth engine&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 million users have experienced the value of using a Menti!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Building on that product-led foundation, Mentimeter is used daily by more than 84.000 organisations globally across all industries and we now serve more than 3,200 Enterprise customers globally. Our next challenge is to increase a systematic enterprise demand growth engine - and we are looking for a VP Enterprise Marketing to lead that journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a global leadership role responsible for how Mentimeter creates, identifies and converts enterprise demand. You will lead our Enterprise Marketing organisation, report to our Chief Sales Officer and join Mentimeter&#39;s Global Enterprise Leadership Team. Your primary focus will be EMEA and North America, while building the foundations for APAC. The goal is to connect our product adoption, organic reach and customer base into an Enterprise qualified pipeline, ARR and customer growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll lead&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead three existing teams, each with an experienced leader, across three connected areas:&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Digital demand&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Build and optimize enterprise demand generation and capture across web, paid media, account-based programs, content distribution, conversion and nurture.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Field and customer marketing&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Develop a global strategy across events, partner programs, customer advocacy, regional activation and use-case storytelling - measured by account engagement, adoption, pipeline and expansion, not simply attendance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Executive Exchange&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Build Mentimeter&#39;s Executive Exchange into a distinctive platform for strategic customers, including our Enterprise Community, executive networks, education and certification programs.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own Mentimeter&#39;s global Enterprise Marketing strategy, budget and operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an integrated system for demand generation and demand capture that turns our PLG footprint and product signals into account-level pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set priorities across segments, accounts, audiences, buying groups, use cases and regions, balancing global consistency with local relevance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create qualified pipeline and measurable Enterprise ARR impact, with clear accountability for conversion, velocity, attribution and ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, coach and develop leaders and senior marketing talent, creating an organisation that performs beyond your direct involvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales, Customer Success, Product, Growth, Brand, Data and regional leadership to strengthen the handover from product-led growth to sales-assisted opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stop, redesign or reallocate investment away from programs that do not create meaningful customer or commercial impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will help you succeed&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an experienced B2B marketing leader who combines strategic range with commercial discipline. You are likely to bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of B2B SaaS marketing experience, including significant leadership experience in Enterprise Marketing, Demand Generation, Integrated Marketing or a closely related area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading leaders and multidisciplinary teams across digital demand, field marketing, customer marketing or executive programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of enterprise buying journeys, account-based marketing, buying groups, demand capture and pipeline creation in a PLG environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience connecting product-led or high-volume inbound growth with a sales-assisted enterprise motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial fluency across funnel economics, pipeline, conversion, attribution, investment and ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating across EMEA and/or North America and adapting global programs to local markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An AI-native approach to marketing: using AI to improve insight, experimentation, personalisation and performance - not only individual productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The kind of leader who will thrive here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You create clarity where ownership is shared and the answer is not obvious. You set a high bar while building trust, develop leaders and give talented people meaningful ownership. Most importantly, you want to build - not simply inherit and administer - a modern Enterprise Marketing function, see the strategy through and be accountable for its long-term impact. You are ambitious while staying humble, curious and collaborative in how you get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have the mandate to shape how Mentimeter approaches enterprise demand globally and define the next chapter of our Enterprise growth. If you are looking for a finished playbook, this probably is not the role for you. If you want to build the system and be accountable for its impact, we would like to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re actively hiring for one position, which can be based in either Stockholm or Toronto. The role follows our hybrid way of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we lead at Mentimeter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mentimeter, we have a Leadership Manifesto that sets a shared direction for how we lead ourselves, our teams and the business. We call it Heart &amp;amp; Bravery.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;It starts with authenticity: knowing yourself, showing yourself and leading yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect our leaders to develop high-performing teams through both care and challenge, drive the right results in a changing environment, and set a clear direction by connecting the work to our vision and making the complex simple.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will learn more about our Leadership Manifesto throughout the recruitment process. These principles are also an important part of how we assess and hire leaders at Mentimeter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our recruitment process&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want the process to be transparent and give both you and us the opportunity to get to know each other properly. The steps are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TA Intro Interview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring Manager Interview:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A 20-minute coffee chat with our Chief Sales Officer to meet and learn more about the role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Case &amp;amp; Competence Interview&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A short business case, submitted the day before the competence interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competence interview: 75-minute at our office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership and culture interview: &lt;/strong&gt;90-minute at our office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;References and a coffee chat&lt;/strong&gt; with the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offer and signing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Mentimeter, we believe in fair and transparent compensation that grows with you. The salary range for this role is SEK 103,000–SEK 135,000 per month. It’s intentionally broad to reflect the different stages of growth within the role: from early development to deep expertise and meaningful impact.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Where an individual is placed within the range depends on factors such as relevant experience, demonstrated skills, and alignment with the role’s requirements. We’re committed to supporting your growth. You’ll have ongoing development conversations with your manager, and your salary will evolve as you build skills and contribute to our mission.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;In addition to your monthly salary, we offer a comprehensive benefits package—learn more about it here: &lt;/em&gt;https://www.mentimeter.com/benefits/stockholm&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Mentimeter can offer&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Mentimeter we can offer a diverse and inclusive work environment supported by smart and driven colleagues. We believe in continuous professional development for all of our colleagues and therefore offer access to a leadership program (including external personal coach) and relevant education to ensure that we continue to be state-of-the-art when it comes to innovating and building Mentimeter. Your place will be in a growing company with lots of career opportunities, working on a beloved product used by more than 300 million people. It’s not all about work though, we also offer a very healthy view on work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All of this comes attached with a competitive compensation and benefits package, including pension contributions. Learn more about our benefits by visiting our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/benefits&quot;&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;AI and Hiring at Mentimeter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Mentimeter, we believe AI helps us work smarter - but it never replaces the human assessment, curiosity, and personal connection that define our culture and our hiring. We use AI as a sparring partner: to bounce ideas, bring new perspectives, support structure, and make our work more efficient. But the meaning, decisions, and interactions always come from people.&amp;nbsp;AI strengthens our work, but it does not define it. At Mentimeter, we’re not building an AI-driven hiring process - we’re building a people-first culture, where technology helps us listen, learn, and grow together.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture at Mentimeter&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Mentimeter we believe in giving everyone a voice - regardless of who you are. So we build a platform that does just that. Our platform is not only our product but also our organization. A platform where people feel safe, where differences are embraced, a place where you can have fun. We strongly encourage applicants who are people of color, LGBTQ+, women, people with disabilities, and/or formerly incarcerated people, and a college degree is not strictly required. In order to give everyone a voice, we need to be as diverse as our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about our culture by visiting our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/culture&quot;&gt;Culture page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Review our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mentimeter.com/trust/legal/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
